            <ArticleTitle>The management of pain in sickle cell disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1029-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>For people with sickle cell disease, vaso-occlusive crisis pain is a frequently encountered problem that poses unique and often perplexing challenges in management. This article reviews the natural history of vaso-occlusive crisis and discusses intervention appropriate for the care of patients with pain due to this chronic illness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
